0..77 Comment "//! Dybjer and Setzer\'s codes for inductive-recursive definitions, as data. A"
78..130 Comment "//! function gives the arguments each code asks for."
131..134 Comment "//!"
135..207 Comment "//! A code describes a family and its decoder at once. A code asks for a"
208..283 Comment "//! value of a type, for values of the family, or for a stop. The values of"
284..353 Comment "//! the family come through their decodes. A stop names one decode. A"
354..431 Comment "//! function computes the type of these arguments from the code. A family and"
432..480 Comment "//! its decoder thus follow from the code alone."
481..484 Comment "//!"
485..562 Comment "//! The codes are a large type. A field of a code holds a type. The pairs are"
563..640 Comment "//! data. The function `args` returns them as terms. It recurses on the code."
641..716 Comment "//! The delta arm asks for a function into the family. The rest of the code"
717..765 Comment "//! reads that function through the decoder `t`."
766..769 Comment "//!"
770..835 Comment "//! - owes: #3575 — the family a code defines, with its decoder"
836..915 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the family a code defines"
916..980 Comment "//!   and its decoder, refused, over the decode of its arguments"
981..1060 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]"
1061..1064 Comment "//!"
1065..1257 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-48959-2_11 \"Dybjer and Setzer, A finite axiomatization of inductive-recursive definitions\""
